# Settings of the production stack (docker-compose.yml).
# Copy to deploy/.env on the server, replace every <...> placeholder, fill in every empty value marked
# REQUIRED, then: chmod 600 .env
# deploy/.env holds secrets: it is git-ignored and must never be committed or sent by mail/chat.
# Values: no quotes needed; do not use the character $ (Compose would read it as a variable).
# Fails closed: with an empty REQUIRED value `docker compose` refuses to start anything ("set
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD in deploy/.env"); with a <...> placeholder left in DOMAIN, SESSION_SECRET or an OIDC_*
# value, or a SESSION_SECRET copied from this repository (dev.env, the tests), the API never serves a
# request: its workers stop at start-up with the reason (repeated in `docker compose logs api`) and the api
# container stays unhealthy. Caddy also refuses a placeholder DOMAIN.

# --- Site ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host name users open, without https:// (DNS A record -> this server). Caddy gets the HTTPS certificate
# for it automatically; the app's PUBLIC_URL becomes https://<domain>.
DOMAIN=<domain>

# --- Database (the stack's own Postgres container, never published on a host port) ------------------
# REQUIRED. Letters and digits only (it is part of the database URL). Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# Optional (defaults: ca / ca):
# POSTGRES_USER=ca
# POSTGRES_DB=ca

# --- Sign-in session ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs the session cookie: at least 32 random characters. Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
# Never reuse a value written anywhere in this repository (the API refuses those). Changing it signs
# everybody out.
SESSION_SECRET=<generate-with-openssl-rand-hex-32>

# --- Microsoft Entra ID (values provided by the reviewer; see backend/README.md "Sign-in (operator)") ----
# Single-tenant app registration. Redirect URI registered on it (platform "Web"):
#   https://<domain>/api/auth/callback
OIDC_ISSUER=https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant-id>/v2.0
OIDC_CLIENT_ID=<client-id>
OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=<client-secret>
# Label of the sign-in button ("Sign in with ..."). Default for Entra: Microsoft
# OIDC_PROVIDER_NAME=Microsoft

# First administrator(s): comma-separated emails that become admin on their FIRST sign-in when they have
# no user row yet. May stay empty: add the first admin with the CLI instead
#   docker compose exec api python -m app.cli add-user <admin-email> --role admin
# After that the CLI is the only way to manage users.
APP_ADMIN_EMAILS=

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Postgres connection pool per uvicorn worker (2 workers):
# DB_POOL_SIZE=5
# DB_MAX_OVERFLOW=5
# DB_POOL_RECYCLE=1800
# A write that waits longer than this for a lock answers HTTP 503 "try again":
# DB_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# Subnet of the Caddy <-> API network; the API trusts X-Forwarded-For only from it. Change it if
# `docker compose up` reports that the address pool overlaps an existing network.
# CA_EDGE_SUBNET=172.29.247.0/24
# Tag of the two images built on the server (e.g. the git commit, so an older tag can be started again).
# CA_TAG=local
# Only for Google sign-in (not used with Entra): comma-separated Workspace domains.
# OIDC_GOOGLE_HD=

# --- Set by docker-compose.yml: do not put these here ---------------------------------------------------
# APP_ENV=production, DATABASE_URL (built from the POSTGRES_* values), PUBLIC_URL (https://DOMAIN),
# FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS (CA_EDGE_SUBNET).
# Never used in production: APP_AUTH (sign-in is always on), APP_CORS_ORIGINS (pages and API share one
# origin, no CORS).
